# Project Fundamentals - Always Apply

You are working on a **Production RAG system using LangGraph** to analyze "How People Use AI" research papers.

## Core Project Context

This is a LangGraph-based RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) system that:
- Processes PDF research papers about AI usage patterns
- Uses local LLM inference via Ollama (gpt-oss:20b for chat, embeddinggemma for embeddings)
- Stores vector embeddings in Qdrant (running in Docker on port 6333)
- Implements a stateful graph workflow with retrieve → generate nodes

## Critical Constants & Configuration

> **⚠️ SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH**: All configuration values defined here. Reference this section from other rules.

### Service Configuration
- **Ollama API URL**: http://localhost:11434
- **Qdrant API URL**: http://localhost:6333
- **Qdrant Dashboard**: http://localhost:6333/dashboard

### Model Configuration
- **Chat model**: gpt-oss:20b
  - **Temperature**: 0.6
  - **Minimum Ollama version**: 0.11.10+
- **Embedding model**: embeddinggemma:latest
  - **Embedding dimension**: 768 - NEVER change this
  - **Distance metric**: Cosine similarity

### Vector Store Configuration
- **Collection name**: "ai_usage_knowledge_index"
- **Retriever k value**: 5 documents
- **Vector size**: 768 (must match embedding dimension)

### Document Processing Configuration
- **Text splitter**: RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter
- **Chunk size**: 750 tokens
- **Chunk overlap**: 0
- **Tokenizer**: tiktoken cl100k_base encoding
- **File glob pattern**: "**/*.pdf"
- **Document loader**: PyMuPDFLoader

### Environment Configuration
- **Python manager**: uv
- **Container orchestration**: docker-compose
- **Jupyter kernel**: venv created by `uv sync`

### LangSmith Configuration (Optional)
- **Tracing variable**: LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2=true
- **Project name**: RAG-Assignment
- **API endpoint**: https://api.smith.langchain.com

